{"step_index":123,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T16:52:26Z","thinking":"Loading a large number of channels into the list widget directly might cause UI freezing; this needs optimization. The current plan involves temporarily disabling updates, adding items in bulk instead of individually, and then re-enabling updates to improve responsiveness.\n\n\nDisabling updates during channel loading significantly improved performance for the list widget. Implementing a debounce timer and minimum character requirement is necessary to prevent lag when searching a large channel list. Moving on to understanding the broadcast hub's architecture, a basic thread-based single-stream broadcaster appears to use a worker thread for fetching and distributing data.\n\n\nThe broadcaster establishes a single, persistent connection to the content source for optimized data retrieval. Data is read in fixed-size blocks and distributed to connected clients. A buffer is maintained for each client to handle potential network latency or temporary client slowdowns; the oldest data is discarded if the buffer is full. This design ensures graceful handling of slow clients while maintaining real-time stream integrity.\n\n\nThe local MPV player and the Xiaomi TV receive identical data chunks from a shared queue, avoiding redundant connections to the content source. The architecture allows seamless channel switching on the TV by updating the local hub with the new stream, with MPV connecting to the local hub for buffering. Furthermore, the HTTP server provides an interactive web remote interface for channel browsing and playback control on various devices and serves the playlist in M3U format.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport urllib.request, threading, time, socket, queue\nfrom http.server import BaseHTTPRequestHandler, ThreadingHTTPServer\n\nq = queue.Queue(maxsize=50)\nstop = threading.Event()\n\ndef upstream():\n    url = 'http://398607.solanaflix.com/live/TV-76173252/624816943106/461946.ts'\n    req = urllib.request.Request(url, headers={'User-Agent': 'VLC/3.0'})\n    with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=10) as r:\n        while not stop.is_set():\n            data = r.read(32768)\n            if not data: break\n            if q.full():\n                try: q.get_nowait()\n                except: pass\n            q.put_nowait(data)\n\nt = threading.Thread(target=upstream, daemon=True)\nt.start()\ntime.sleep(1)\nprint('Upstream queue size:', q.qsize())\nstop.set()\n\" 2>&1","Cwd":"/home/slone","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Testing BroadcastHub upstream reader","toolSummary":"Probar lector de flujo upstream del canal"}}]}
